{
  "_comment": [
    "E7 message-string layer — THE canonical exception-message table.",
    "Single source of truth for the C1C3C4 message conjunct's literals:",
    "  * verification/gen-message-data.py generates MessageData.lean from the",
    "    `templates` section (CI regenerates + diffs — the gen-dict-data.py",
    "    drift-gate pattern), and C1C3C4Outcome.lean's model builds its",
    "    messages from MessageData, so a table edit FORCES the Lean gate to",
    "    re-evaluate (the transcribed-literal drift of the 3.14 oracle bump",
    "    cannot recur).",
    "  * verification/message_shipped_binding.py runs every `witnesses` row",
    "    through the REAL `pyths` binary AND the pinned CPython oracle and",
    "    asserts both terminal messages equal the instantiated template — so",
    "    a runtime message change turns the differential red or forces the",
    "    table (and hence the Lean side) to move with it.",
    "Probed live on CPython 3.14.7 (py -3.14), 2026-08-27. The 3.12-era",
    "false-world wordings (legacy312ArithMsg etc.) are deliberately NOT here:",
    "they are refuted worlds and stay inline in C1C3C4Outcome.lean."
  ],
  "oracle": "cpython-3.14.7",
